Package: xppen-uclogic
Version: 1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: anindra <anindra@localhost>
Depends: kmod
Conflicts: xppenlinux, opentabletdriver
Description: Enable kernel hid_uclogic driver for XP-Pen / UC-Logic drawing tablets
 Many XP-Pen, UGEE, Huion, Artisul and VEIKK drawing tablets are supported by
 the in-kernel hid_uclogic driver. However some vendors' userspace drivers and
 OpenTabletDriver blacklist hid_uclogic, which leaves the tablet bound to the
 generic hid-generic driver. In that state the pen produces no events, so the
 cursor does not move and there is no pressure under Wayland.
 .
 This package:
  * ensures the hid_uclogic module is loaded at boot and immediately, and
  * removes any "blacklist hid_uclogic" entry,
 so the tablet is exposed as a real graphics tablet to libinput/KWin and works
 under a Wayland session with pressure, tilt, buttons and eraser.
 .
 Tested with an XP-Pen Deco 01 V2 (28bd:0905) on KDE Plasma 6 (Wayland).
 Note: this package intentionally Conflicts with xppenlinux (X11-only vendor
 driver) and opentabletdriver (which blacklists hid_uclogic).
